Iron has greater affinity for oxygen than copper.

\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{Cu}_2 \mathrm{O}+\mathrm{FeS} \rightarrow \mathrm{FeO}+\mathrm{Cu}_2 \mathrm{~S} \\
\mathrm{FeO}+\mathrm{SiO}_2 \rightarrow \mathrm{FeSiO}_3 \\
(\mathrm{slag})
\end{gathered}

\begin{aligned}
& 2 \mathrm{Cu}_2 \mathrm{~S}+3 \mathrm{O}_2 \rightarrow 2 \mathrm{Cu}_2 \mathrm{O}+2 \mathrm{SO}_2 \\
& 2 \mathrm{Cu}_2 \mathrm{O}+\mathrm{Cu}_2 \mathrm{~S} \underset{\text { auto }}{\text { reduction }} 6 \mathrm{Cu}+\mathrm{SO}_2 .
\end{aligned}
